","sponsorshipDate":"2025-01-09","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"OK"},{"bioguideId":"M001212","fullName":"Rep. Moore, Barry [R-AL-1]","isOriginalCosponsor":true,"party":"R","sponsorshipDate":"2025-01-09","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"AL"},{"bioguideId":"L000596","fullName":"Rep. Luna, Anna Paulina [R-FL-13]","isOriginalCosponsor":true,"party":"R","sponsorshipDate":"2025-01-09","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"FL"},{"bioguideId":"C001051","fullName":"Rep. Carter, John R. [R-TX-31]","isOriginalCosponsor":false,"party":"R","sponsorshipDate":"2025-01-14","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"TX"},{"bioguideId":"H001086","fullName":"Rep. Harshbarger, Diana [R-TN-1]","isOriginalCosponsor":false,"party":"R","sponsorshipDate":"2025-01-21","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"TN"},{"bioguideId":"H001102","fullName":"Rep. Harris, Mark [R-NC-8]","isOriginalCosponsor":false,"party":"R","sponsorshipDate":"2025-02-04","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"NC"},{"bioguideId":"G000601","fullName":"Rep. Goldman, Craig [R-TX-12]","isOriginalCosponsor":false,"party":"R","sponsorshipDate":"2025-02-04","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"TX"},{"bioguideId":"M001240","fullName":"Rep. McDowell, Addison [R-NC-6]","isOriginalCosponsor":false,"party":"R","sponsorshipDate":"2025-02-26","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"NC"},{"bioguideId":"S001196","fullName":"Rep. Stefanik, Elise M. [R-NY-21]","isOriginalCosponsor":false,"party":"R","sponsorshipDate":"2025-04-07","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"NY"},{"bioguideId":"B001325","fullName":"Rep. Biggs, Sheri [R-SC-3]","isOriginalCosponsor":false,"party":"R","sponsorshipDate":"2026-02-04","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"SC"},{"bioguideId":"G000568","fullName":"Rep. Griffith, H. Morgan [R-VA-9]","isOriginalCosponsor":false,"party":"R","sponsorshipDate":"2026-04-27","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"VA"}],"fetchedAt":"2026-09-16T18:56:55+00:00","id":"hr318-119","introducedDate":"2025-01-09","latestAction":{"actionDate":"2025-01-09","text":"Referred to the Subcommittee on Border Security and Enforcement."},"laws":[],"number":"318","originChamber":"House","policyArea":"Immigration","sponsors":[{"bioguideId":"R000614","district":21,"fullName":"Rep. Roy, Chip [R-TX-21]","party":"R","state":"TX"}],"summaries":[{"actionDate":"2025-01-09","actionDesc":"Introduced in House","text":"<p><strong>Border Safety and Security Act of 2025</strong></p><p>This bill requires the Department of Homeland Security (DHS) to suspend the entry of any non-U.S. nationals (<em>aliens</em> under federal law) without valid entry documents during any period when DHS cannot detain such an individual or return the individual to a foreign country contiguous to the United States. A state may sue DHS to enforce this requirement.</p><p>(Under current law, non-U.S. nationals who arrive at the border without entry documents are generally subject to expedited removal. However, if such an individual is found to have a credible fear of persecution, they are typically subject to detention while their asylum claim is being considered.)</p><p>The bill also authorizes DHS to suspend the entry of non-U.S. nationals without entry documents at the border if DHS determines that such a suspension is necessary to achieve operational control over such a border.</p>","updateDate":"2025-02-27T18:39:27Z","versionCode":"00"}],"title":"Border Safety and Security Act of 2025","type":"hr","updateDate":"2026-07-18T00:04:24Z","updateDateIncludingText":"2026-07-18T00:04:24Z"}
